      "content": "In the 5.5 to 7.0 pH range, soil acidity generally promotes the solubility and subsequent availability of micronutrients like iron ($\\text{Fe}$) and manganese ($\\text{Mn}$) for grapevine uptake. As pH rises above this range, these divalent cations become less soluble and precipitate, leading to potential deficiencies. Staying within this range helps maintain a critical balance where these essential elements are readily accessible to the vine's root system for physiological function.",
