    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. To go a bit deeper, could you explain the specific chemical mechanism behind why higher pH causes that precipitation? Like, what's actually happening at the soil-root interface to make those nutrients stop being available? I want to be able to explain the 'why' to the owner so they get why we can't let it drift too high.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
