      "content": "Got it, so it's basically a chemical lockout. Given that, if the grower sees signs of manganese deficiency—like interveinal chlorosis on younger leaves—but the soil test shows manganese is actually present, what are the most likely environmental or management factors that could be causing this \"hidden\" deficiency despite the levels being technically okay?",
